{"url": "https://gsbs.utsouthwestern.edu/programs/curriculum/", "final_url": "https://gsbs.utsouthwestern.edu/programs/curriculum/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "UT Southwestern Graduate School Curriculum - UT Southwestern, Dallas, Texas\nSkip to Main\nBack to\nUT Southwestern Home\nAll\nPatient Care\nEducation & Training\nResearch\nFaculty\nDepartments & Centers\nNewsroom\nEvents\nAbout Us\nEmployees\nHome\nPrograms\nCurrent:Curriculum\nGraduate School of Biomedical Sciences\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nFinancial Support\nAdmissions\nResearch Opportunities\nCareer Development\nContact Us\nRequest More Info\nCurriculum\nCore (BSS)\nRCR\nNanocourses\nT32 Training Programs\nCurriculum\nBasic Biomedical Sciences (BBS) program\nEight of the basic science Ph.D. programs are united under one umbrella program that admits a single cohort of first-year students. The list includes Biological Chemistry, Cancer Biology, Cell and Molecular Biology, Genetics Development and Disease, Immunology, Molecular Biophysics, Molecular Microbiology, and Neuroscience.\nYear 1: Common Curriculum & Specialization\nShared Foundation: Students complete a common curriculum consisting of a core course, a minimum of two laboratory rotations, and thorough training in the responsible conduct of research.\nProgram Selection: During the second semester, students typically transition into their chosen individual Ph.D. programs.\nYear 2: Candidacy & Dissertation Committee\nQualifying Exam: Students take an exam to officially become a candidate for a Ph.D. in their selected program.\nCommittee Assembly: Students are expected to assemble a dissertation committee of faculty members who will oversee their research throughout the remainder of their training.\nIndependent Curricula\nEach degree program below features separate and independent curricula. The programs may share some elements of the Basic Biomedical Sciences (BBS) umbrella program. View the individual program tiles below for program-wise details.\nBasic Biomedical Sciences (BBS)\nBiomedical Engineering (BME)\nOrganic Chemistry (OC)\nMedical Physics (MPHYS)\nClinical Psychology (CLP)\nBiomedical Education\nResponsible Conduct of Research\nNanocourses\nT32 Training Programs\nNOTE: Clinical Psychology Ph.D. students do NOT participate in the Basic Science Core Curriculum. The Clinical Psychology Program admits first-year students directly into their APA-accredited training program with a separate curriculum.\nApply Now Online\nAdmission Requirements\nBack-to top\nFooter Links\nInstitution\nResearch\nClinical Trials\nCore Facilities\nCTSA Program\nPostdoctoral Scholars\nResearch Administration\nResearch Labs\nResearch Programs\nScientific Discoveries\nTechnology Development\nEducation & Training\nCME\nDepartments\nEducation Programs\nGraduate School\nGME\nLibrary\nMedical School\nSchool of Health Professions\nSchool of Public Health\nStudent Support\nWellness & Counseling\nPatient Care\nConditions & Treatments\nFind a Doctor\nLocations\nMedBlog\nMyChart\nPatient Resources\nPhysician Resources\nPrice Transparency\nRequest an Appointment\nNewsroom\nNews Releases\nMedia Relations\nAbout Us\nAdministrative Offices\nCareers\nComments\nContact Us\nFaculty Directory\nGiving\nLeadership\nMaps & Directions\nOffice of the President\nPhone Directory\nSitemap\nTitle IX\nLegal\nHEERF Reporting\nNon-Discrimination Policy\nOpen Records\nPatient Rights\nPrivacy Policy\nProtected Expression\nSite Policies\nState\nState of Texas\nTexas Veterans Portal\nTRAIL Search\nUT System\nSocial\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYoutube\nPinterest\nLinkedIn\nStudent Mental Health Resources\nInstitutional Resume\nCopyright 2024. The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center\n5323 Harry Hines Blvd., Dallas, Texas 75390 Phone 214-648-3111", "links": [["Skip to Main", "https://gsbs.utsouthwestern.edu/programs/curriculum/#page_main"], ["Back to UT Southwestern Home", "https://www.utsouthwestern.edu"], ["Home", "https:/